root/div[0]/main[0]/div[2]/div[1]/article[4]/div[0]/h3[0]/text "What the same budget could generate when moved to products that sell"
root/div[0]/main[0]/div[2]/div[1]/article[4]/div[0]/p[0]
root/div[0]/main[0]/div[2]/div[1]/article[4]/div[0]/p[0]/text "+€900"
root/div[0]/main[0]/div[2]/div[1]/article[4]/div[0]/p[1]
root/div[0]/main[0]/div[2]/div[1]/article[4]/div[0]/p[1]/text "Products that actually sell return 18.00 times their spend and currently generate 900 EUR. If weak products are stopped and that 1,200 EUR is moved to them — without adding budget — they could reach 1,800 EUR. The calculation is capped at twice current sales, even though a simple multiplication would give more: strong products have limited search volume and cannot absorb unlimited budget at the same return. This is an optimistic ceiling, not a promise: returns usually decline as budget increases. These are sales, not profit — profit depends on your margin."
